More generally, every simply connected output in these $17$ rows,
with arbitrary data \eqref{maps:eq:D.SC1}, is oriented diffeomorphic to
\begin{equation}
                              \widetilde\Sigma_0N_M,         \hypertarget{tag-0244}{}\label{maps:eq:D.SC6}
\end{equation}
with the twisted framing and the Smale five-manifold of \SeriesRef{maps:src:D.2.14}.
Thus its full smooth type depends only on $M$, including when $M$
is even. For $b>1$, \eqref{maps:eq:D.SC2}--\eqref{maps:eq:D.SC3} give the complete integral
homology, with \eqref{maps:eq:D.SC4} in the simply connected cases.
Every such output is excluded by the sphere criterion.

