For the other composite choose any integer representative $b_{\rm hom}$ of
the second coordinate in \eqref{maps:eq:IC_local_15}, put $z_{\rm aug}=x-sRx$, and write
\begin{equation}
 k_{\rm hom}=\frac{t-b_{\rm hom}-c^t\mathcal K z_{\rm aug}}{h}\in\mathbb Z.
 \label{maps:eq:IC_local_18}
\end{equation}
The error has the exact integral boundary preimage
\begin{equation}
 (x,t)-(sRx,b_{\rm hom})=d_3(0,\mathcal K z_{\rm aug}+k_{\rm hom}\eta).
 \label{maps:eq:IC_local_19}
\end{equation}
This proves $\Psi\Phi=I$. It also supplies a preimage for every
zero class: take $Rx=0$ and $b_{\rm hom}=0$ in \eqref{maps:eq:IC_local_18}--\eqref{maps:eq:IC_local_19}.

